{"duration_api_ms":81635,"stop_reason":"end_turn","session_id":"d1135da2-c9e6-446b-aaf3-6198f32e61f3","total_cost_usd":0.304776,"usage":{"input_tokens":16,"cache_creation_input_tokens":18884,"cache_read_input_tokens":196760,"output_tokens":8547,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":1552},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":18884},"inference_geo":"global","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":909,"cache_read_input_tokens":31852,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1634,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":1634,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard","fallback_credit":null},"modelUsage":{"claude-opus-5-5":{"inputTokens":16,"outputTokens":8547,"cacheReadInputTokens":196760,"cacheCreationInputTokens":18884,"webSearchRequests":0,"costUSD":0.304776,"contextWindow":1000000,"maxOutputTokens":128000,"thinkingTokens":1552,"cacheCreationEphemeral5mInputTokens":18884,"cacheCreationEphemeral1hInputTokens":0,"canonicalModel":"claude-opus-5-5","provider":"firstParty","costBasis":"list"}},"permission_denials":[{"tool_name":"Bash","tool_use_id":"toolu_01JkeNFfP5K1hjJ8Be8Y6jAX","tool_input":{"command":"cd /tmp && python3 -I -c \"\nfrom decimal import Decimal, ROUND_HALF_UP, localcontext\ndef r(v,n=0):\n    d=Decimal(repr(v)) if isinstance(v,float) else Decimal(v)\n    q=Decimal(1).scaleb(-n)\n    with localcontext() as c:\n        c.prec=max(28, len(d.as_tuple().digits)+abs(d.as_tuple().exponent)+abs(n)+2)\n        res=d.quantize(q, rounding=ROUND_HALF_UP)\n    return int(res) if n<=0 else float(res)\nfor a in [(3.7,),(3.2,),(3.14159,2),(3.14159,3),(1234,-2),(1250,-2),(-1250,-2),(2.5,),(0.5,),(-2.5,),(-0.5,),(0.125,2),(-0.125,2),(2.675,2),(1.005,2),(7,),(7,2),(2.4,1),(10**40,),(1e300,-2),(0.1,400),(1e-300,2),(5,-3)]:\n    x=r(*a); print(a,x,type(x).__name__)\n\"","description":"Prototype rounding approach to validate criteria"}}],"terminal_reason":"completed","fast_mode_state":"off","fast_mode_disabled_reason":"sdk_opt_in_required","subagent_stats":{"spawned":0,"requested":{"background":0,"foreground":0,"unset":0},"started_in_background":0,"max_depth":0,"spawned_by_subagents":0,"completed":0,"failed":0,"killed":{"parent":0,"user":0,"system":0},"refused":{"depth_limit":0,"concurrency_limit":0,"budget":0},"by_type":{}},"safety_stops":0,"is_error":false,"num_turns":9,"subtype":"success","api_error_status":null,"result":"I've written `design.md` and `constraints.json` (14 constraints) to `.dark-factory/runs/e60eb29f-c3d2-44f4-9f43-99eebdccd5cb/artifacts/ARCHITECTURE/`. Running Python here wasn't permitted, so the rounding approach hasn't been run. I checked it by hand against every example in the acceptance criteria.\n\n**The design:**\n- **What changes:** one new function, `round_number(value: int | float, ndigits: int = 0) -> int | float`, added below `add` in `src/app_int/main.py`. It uses only the standard library, `pyproject.toml` stays as it is, and `health_check`, `add` and `tests/test_main.py` are left alone.\n- **How it rounds:**\n  1. Reject bad input types with `TypeError`: a `bool` or a non-number for `value`, and a `bool` or non-`int` for `ndigits`.\n  2. Reject NaN and ±infinity with `ValueError`.\n  3. Convert the value to a `Decimal` from its displayed form, `repr(value)`. This is what makes `2.675` round to `2.68`; converting the float directly would round it to `2.67`.\n  4. Round with `ROUND_HALF_UP`. Despite the name, Python's decimal module defines this as half away from zero for both signs.\n  5. Return an `int` when `ndigits <= 0` and a `float` when `ndigits > 0`.\n- **Large inputs:** very large numbers or a large `ndigits` would make the decimal module raise an error at its default precision. The rounding step runs in a temporary decimal context with a higher precision, so global settings are never changed and the function stays side-effect free.\n- **Who writes what:** the Developer may only edit under `src/**`, so the tests required by AC-18 (and the checks for AC-1 to AC-14) are assigned to QA. The suggested file is `tests/test_round_number.py`.\n\n**Decisions to be aware of:**\n- When an input is invalid in more than one way, the order is value type, then `ndigits` type, then NaN/infinity. For example, `round_number(nan, \"1\")` raises `TypeError`.\n- Rounding a huge int (above about 1.8e308) with `ndigits > 0` returns `float('inf')`. No criterion covers this, so it is left unhandled.\n\nThe two open questions from the BA are carried forward unchanged: whether to accept `Decimal` input (assumed no) and whether half-away-from-zero is the preferred tie rule (assumed yes). Either can be changed later without changing the signature, so nothing blocks the Developer.","ttft_ms":2855,"type":"result","duration_ms":82079,"uuid":"64ab793d-e0da-4994-81d7-05f50b9af5d5","ttft_stream_ms":1689,"time_to_request_ms":315,"first_content_frame_ms":1690,"queued_turn_count":0,"result_index":0}
